<configuration xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="http://sumo.dlr.de/xsd/sumoConfiguration.xsd">
  <!-- Predictive-routing co-simulation WITH the event overlay (RQ3 / paper 2),
       test day 2023-07-04. Driven by FleetPy via
       fleetpy/src/coupling/SUMO/SUMOFleetPyServer.py, NOT by the vaas run.py.

       Identical to 2023-07-04_rq3_cosim.sumocfg except that
       2023-07-04_rq3_event_corridor.add.xml is appended to additional-files,
       applying the corridor-scale lane blockage from 13:00 to 14:00 (Manchinger Strasse, the arterial carrying the largest share of AMoD trips (12.1%). 115 edges, 145 lanes closed).
       Everything else (calibration, background demand, amod vType) is held
       fixed so the event and no-event cells differ in one factor only.

       run_rq3_routing.sh selects this config for any cell whose scenario name
       carries `_evt`, and fails loudly if it is missing rather than falling
       back to the no-event config.

       ⚠️ ignore-route-errors is NOT set here. SUMOFleetPyServer builds its own
       command line, so the flag has to be passed there; a lane blockage can
       leave a PT vehicle with no path to its fixed stop, which would otherwise
       abort the whole co-simulation.

       Note that SUMOFleetPyServer passes its generated edgeData config via -a,
       and SUMO's -a REPLACES this list rather than extending it; the server
       merges these entries back in (src/coupling/SUMO/sumocfg_utils.py).
       Without that merge the traffic lights, WAUT, public transport and this
       event add-file are all silently dropped, which would produce a no-event
       run under an event name. -->
  <input>
    <net-file value="ingolstadt_net.net.xml" />
    <route-files value="Routes/routes_2023-07-04_24h_det_calib.rou.xml.gz" />
    <additional-files value="TL/2023-07-04_tlLogics_24h.tll.xml, TL/2023-07-04_WAUT.xml, PT/pt_stops.add.xml, PT/2023-07-04_gtfs_trips.rou.xml, rq3_amod_vtype.add.xml, 2023-07-04_rq3_event_corridor.add.xml" />
  </input>
  <time>
    <begin value="00:00:00" />
    <end value="24:00:00" />
  </time>
  <processing>
    <step-length value="1" />
    <scale value="0.85" />
    <ignore-junction-blocker value="15" />
    <time-to-teleport value="60" />
    <max-depart-delay value="100" />
    <device.rerouting.probability value="0.5" />
  </processing>
</configuration>
